WEBVTT

1
00:00:10.881 --> 00:00:15.084
Peter was enjoying breakfast in his favorite spot, in front of the kitchen window.

2
00:00:15.104 --> 00:00:18.967
"It's 7:15," Grandma said.

3
00:00:18.987 --> 00:00:21.930
"Shouldn't you leave for school?"

4
00:00:23.231 --> 00:00:25.493
She was staying with Peter while his parents were away.

5
00:00:25.513 --> 00:00:28.635
"I can leave at 7:25 and not be late!"

6
00:00:28.915 --> 00:00:29.416
Peter said.

7
00:00:30.304 --> 00:00:32.846
"It's the best thing about living across the street from school."

8
00:00:34.206 --> 00:00:36.748
Just then they heard the screech of tires outside.

9
00:00:37.648 --> 00:00:41.671
Grandma looked out the window and saw a car stopped in the middle of the intersection.

10
00:00:42.691 --> 00:00:46.073
The driver leaned out the window to scold a girl from Peter's class.

11
00:00:47.074 --> 00:00:49.475
Peter could easily guess what the driver was saying.

12
00:00:49.495 --> 00:00:54.498
He imitated him aloud: "Look where you're going, not at your phone!"

13
00:00:54.518 --> 00:00:57.320
"He's right," Grandma said.

14
00:00:58.240 --> 00:01:01.042
"You have to look up when crossing the street."

15
00:01:01.062 --> 00:01:03.663
"I know," Peter said.

16
00:01:03.683 --> 00:01:06.785
"But kids get distracted by their phones."

17
00:01:07.866 --> 00:01:08.706
Grandma frowned.

18
00:01:08.726 --> 00:01:12.969
"Something should be done before someone gets hurt."

19
00:01:15.550 --> 00:01:19.673
That day in art class, the teacher asked the students to create a public-service ad.

20
00:01:19.693 --> 00:01:24.876
"Make a sign that helps solve a problem in our community," she instructed.

21
00:01:25.932 --> 00:01:28.654
Peter thought back to the incident at the intersection that morning.

22
00:01:30.435 --> 00:01:34.177
"I don't know if it will help," he thought, "but I have an idea."

23
00:01:35.458 --> 00:01:37.098
He painted the words "Look Up!"

24
00:01:37.479 --> 00:01:39.400
in bright colors on a large board.

25
00:01:40.240 --> 00:01:42.261
Then he drew two pictures on the sign.

26
00:01:43.422 --> 00:01:46.944
One picture showed a person staring at a cell phone while crossing the street.

27
00:01:48.065 --> 00:01:50.606
Nearby a car was slamming on its brakes.

28
00:01:51.627 --> 00:01:53.628
Peter painted a red line through the picture.

29
00:01:54.772 --> 00:01:57.154
The other picture was another person crossing the street.

30
00:01:58.034 --> 00:01:59.756
This person's eyes were focused ahead.

31
00:02:00.836 --> 00:02:02.578
A car patiently waited at the light.

32
00:02:03.458 --> 00:02:05.860
"Great sign, Peter," the teacher said.

33
00:02:05.880 --> 00:02:07.661
"What inspired it?"

34
00:02:08.382 --> 00:02:10.383
Peter explained the problem at the intersection.

35
00:02:10.403 --> 00:02:13.705
"I almost got hit crossing there yesterday!"

36
00:02:14.086 --> 00:02:14.886
a girl exclaimed.

37
00:02:14.906 --> 00:02:17.408
"Were you looking at your phone?"

38
00:02:17.748 --> 00:02:18.509
the teacher asked.

39
00:02:18.529 --> 00:02:21.691
"I was watching a funny video."

40
00:02:22.191 --> 00:02:22.972
The girl shrugged.

41
00:02:23.988 --> 00:02:25.629
"I didn't want to miss the ending."

42
00:02:25.649 --> 00:02:29.851
"Drivers should watch out for us," another student said.

43
00:02:29.871 --> 00:02:32.273
"True," the teacher said.

44
00:02:32.293 --> 00:02:36.335
"But pedestrians also need to watch out for oncoming traffic.

45
00:02:36.735 --> 00:02:37.816
Nice work, Peter."

46
00:02:38.796 --> 00:02:42.318
The teacher gave Peter his sign to take home and an A for the assignment.

47
00:02:43.599 --> 00:02:47.621
After school Peter set his sign up so anyone crossing the intersection would see it.

48
00:02:48.582 --> 00:02:52.044
But moments later, Principal Axworth came and removed the sign.

49
00:02:53.600 --> 00:02:55.342
"Who put this here and why?"

50
00:02:55.642 --> 00:02:56.183
he growled.

51
00:02:57.103 --> 00:02:57.744
Peter gulped.

52
00:02:59.566 --> 00:03:02.929
He was too intimidated to reply, but he wasn't ready to give up.

53
00:03:03.829 --> 00:03:07.953
He knew he was going to need a strong argument to convince the principal to keep the sign.

54
00:03:09.174 --> 00:03:13.758
Every morning for the rest of the week, Peter counted the number of honks and near-miss collisions.

55
00:03:14.679 --> 00:03:19.584
He calculated the average number of kids crossing the street and how many were looking at their phones.

56
00:03:21.228 --> 00:03:24.489
He also researched real-world statistics on traffic accidents.

57
00:03:25.670 --> 00:03:29.532
Finally he put his findings into a colorful chart comparing all his data.

58
00:03:30.672 --> 00:03:34.274
Now all he had to do was summon the courage to talk to Principal Axworth!

59
00:03:36.414 --> 00:03:39.556
Peter went to school early Monday morning to see Principal Axworth.

60
00:03:40.536 --> 00:03:42.617
Peter explained the problem at the intersection.

61
00:03:43.618 --> 00:03:47.279
Using his chart, he showed the average daily number of kids crossing the street.

62
00:03:48.300 --> 00:03:51.505
He shared his data on how many kids were looking at their phones.

63
00:03:52.466 --> 00:03:55.588
Then he presented the number of car honks and near misses.

64
00:03:56.849 --> 00:04:04.034
"Studies show that while traffic accidents are decreasing, cell phone-related pedestrian accidents are increasing," Peter explained.

65
00:04:04.054 --> 00:04:09.258
"People get so distracted by their phones, they become unaware of their surroundings.

66
00:04:10.579 --> 00:04:13.020
I thought a bright sign would remind students to look up."

67
00:04:13.040 --> 00:04:18.184
"You've prepared a persuasive argument," the principal said.

68
00:04:19.244 --> 00:04:20.366
"We'll put your sign back up.

69
00:04:21.347 --> 00:04:24.932
And I'm going to suggest other schools in the city start a similar program."

70
00:04:26.073 --> 00:04:26.934
Peter beamed.

71
00:04:28.036 --> 00:04:31.100
His sign really was going to help solve a community problem!
